# Checks for the C files, run from this folder:
#   clang-tidy checkers/cchk.c search/csearch.c -- -fopenmp -I checkers/portable -I checkers/portable/noomp
# Left out: advice to use the optional Annex K functions (fprintf_s, memcpy_s, ...); reports about
# signed char tokens, which are small integers and not characters; integer widening in index arithmetic;
# fscanf number conversion (the return values are checked, and the input files are written by
# run_search.py); the bounded recursion over hallways in cchk.c; and style checks.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  misc-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-signed-char-misuse,
  -bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion,
  -cert-err33-c,
  -cert-err34-c,
  -cert-str34-c,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-no-recursion
